    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d365-a1">

                <pb facs="0664" n="564" sameAs="frus:frus1880/pg564"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 112.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Barrington to Mr. Hoppin.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-11-24"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 24,
                        1879</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Hoppin</hi>: Lord Salisbury desires roe to
                    express his regret that lie should not yet have been able to send a reply to
                    your government in the case of the Fortune Bay claims. It is receiving his best
                    attention, but as it was necessary to refer to the governor of Newfoundland for
                    a report, which has only just been received, he fears some time must elapse
                    before he can make a communication on the subject.</p>
                <p>I am yours, very truly,</p>
                <closer><signed>ERIC BARRINGTON.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>An official note to this effect ought to reach you without delay.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
